ANNUAL   8760                                      5.38      1.25     4.48

WHAT THIS IS, AND WHAT IT RESTS ON
   hours-weighted annual total-power reduction  : 5.38 %
   hours-weighted annual makeup water reduction : 1.25 %
   hours-weighted annual cost reduction         : 4.48 %

   Those three are means of ratios. As RATIOS OF ANNUAL TOTALS,
   which is what a plant actually banks over a year:
   annual electrical energy reduction           : 4.52 %   (-0.85 pts)
   annual makeup water reduction                : 2.37 %   (+1.12 pts)
   annual operating cost reduction              : 4.17 %   (-0.32 pts)
   The energy and water corrections have OPPOSITE signs, because
   the energy saving is biggest when the plant draws least power
   and the water saving is biggest when it evaporates most.
   for comparison, the five-condition unweighted mean the V5 gate
   scores                                        : 4.38 % water

   fraction of the weighted year INSIDE the validated wet-bulb
   envelope (<= 21.9 C)                        : 62.5 %
   fraction resting on EXTRAPOLATION            : 37.5 %


   AND WHAT THE EXTRAPOLATION IS ACTUALLY WORTH -- defect 48.
   Reporting the extrapolated FRACTION is not the same as reporting
   what it CARRIES, and here they point opposite ways:

                                   hours   water %  energy %   cost %
   whole year                       8760      2.37      4.52     4.17
   inside the validated envelope    5475     -3.31      8.84     5.32
   EXTRAPOLATED (wb > 21.9 C)       3285      8.23     -0.39     2.90

   THE WATER SAVING IS NEGATIVE WHERE THE MODEL HAS BEEN VALIDATED.
   Every positive water hour is an hour hotter and wetter than any
   data we hold. The ENERGY saving is the opposite -- it is earned
   inside the envelope and vanishes outside it. So the two halves of
   the product are validated to opposite degrees, and the water
   claim is the one that cannot be defended from this dataset.

   That second number is the honest caveat on the first. Roughly
   two fifths of a Dhahran year is hotter and wetter than anything
   the model was validated against, and no amount of weighting
   changes that. It is what the KFUPM wind tunnel is for.

